      "problem": "What are the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola $y=2(x-2)^{2}-12?$",
      "worked_solution": "Remember that the vertex form of a parabola is \n\n$$\ny=a(x-h)^{2}+k,\n$$\n\nwhere $(h,k)$ are the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola.\n\nThe given parabola\n\n$$\ny=2(x-2)^{2}-12\n$$\n\nis written in vertex form with $h=2$ and $k=-12.$ \n\nTherefore, the vertex of the parabola is at $(2,-12).$",
